WEBVTT

00:00.409 --> 00:01.638
- [Voiceover] The rate

00:01.638 --> 00:04.124
at which rainwater flows into a drainpipe

00:04.124 --> 00:05.666
is modeled by the function R,

00:05.666 --> 00:09.847
where R of t is equal
to 20sin of t squared

00:09.847 --> 00:13.723
over 35 cubic feet per hour.

00:13.723 --> 00:18.042
t is measured in hours and 0
is less than or equal to t,

00:18.042 --> 00:19.541
which is less than or equal to 8,

00:19.541 --> 00:21.931
so t is gonna go between 0 and 8.

00:21.931 --> 00:23.419
The pipe is partially blocked,

00:23.419 --> 00:26.518
allowing water to drain out the other end

00:26.518 --> 00:29.710
of the pipe at rate modeled by D of t.

00:29.710 --> 00:33.124
It's equal to -0.04t to the third power

00:33.124 --> 00:38.124
plus 0.4t squared plus
0.96t cubic feet per hour.

00:38.695 --> 00:40.844
For the same interval right over here,

00:40.844 --> 00:44.304
there are 30 cubic feet
of water in the pipe

00:44.304 --> 00:47.097
at time t equals 0.

00:47.097 --> 00:48.205
Alright, Part A.

00:48.205 --> 00:51.335
How many cubic feet of rainwater

00:51.335 --> 00:52.629
flow into the pipe

00:52.629 --> 00:55.288
during the 8 hour time interval

00:55.288 --> 00:57.471
0 is less than or equal to t

00:57.471 --> 00:59.395
is less than or equal to 8?

00:59.395 --> 01:02.064
Alright, so we know the rate,

01:02.064 --> 01:06.235
the rate that things flow
into the rainwater pipe.

01:08.115 --> 01:09.544
Let me draw a little rainwater pipe here

01:09.544 --> 01:11.531
just so that we can
visualize what's going on.

01:12.601 --> 01:16.377
So if that is the pipe right over there,

01:16.377 --> 01:18.866
things are flowing in

01:18.866 --> 01:22.316
at a rate of R of t,

01:22.316 --> 01:27.180
and things are flowing
out at a rate of D of t.

01:27.180 --> 01:30.292
And they even tell us that
there is 30 cubic feet

01:30.292 --> 01:32.370
of water right in the beginning.

01:32.370 --> 01:34.738
But these are the rates of
entry and the rates of exiting.

01:36.098 --> 01:39.650
So they're asking how many
cubic feet of water flow into,

01:39.650 --> 01:44.091
so enter into the pipe, during
the 8-hour time interval.

01:44.091 --> 01:45.727
So if you have your rate,

01:45.727 --> 01:49.269
this is the rate at which
things are flowing into it,

01:49.269 --> 01:51.242
they give it in cubic feet per hour.

01:51.242 --> 01:55.160
If you multiply times some change in time,

01:55.160 --> 01:59.374
even an infinitesimally
small change in time, so Dt,

01:59.374 --> 02:01.243
this is the amount that flows in

02:01.243 --> 02:03.612
over that very small change in time.

02:03.612 --> 02:05.121
And so what we wanna do

02:05.121 --> 02:08.383
is we wanna sum up these amounts

02:08.383 --> 02:10.787
over very small changes in time

02:10.787 --> 02:14.200
to go from time is equal to 0,

02:14.200 --> 02:17.265
all the way to time is equal to 8.

02:17.265 --> 02:19.229
So this expression right over here,

02:19.229 --> 02:20.760
this is going to give us

02:20.760 --> 02:23.129
how many cubic feet of
water flow into the pipe.

02:23.129 --> 02:24.465
Once again, what am I doing?

02:24.465 --> 02:27.483
R of t times D of t,
this is how much flows,

02:27.483 --> 02:31.627
what volume flows in over
a very small interval, dt,

02:31.627 --> 02:32.927
and then we're gonna sum it up

02:32.927 --> 02:35.226
from t equals 0 to t equals 8.

02:35.226 --> 02:37.606
That's the power of the definite integral.

02:37.606 --> 02:39.963
And so this is going to be equal to

02:39.963 --> 02:44.963
the integral from 0 to 8 of 20sin

02:45.040 --> 02:47.997
of t squared

02:47.997 --> 02:52.948
over 35 dt.

02:52.948 --> 02:55.627
And lucky for us we can use calculators

02:55.627 --> 02:57.439
in this section of the AP exam,

02:57.439 --> 03:00.747
so let's bring out a graphing calculator

03:00.747 --> 03:03.505
where we can evaluate definite integrals.

03:03.505 --> 03:04.494
And so let's see.

03:04.494 --> 03:05.403
We wanna do definite integrals

03:05.403 --> 03:09.079
so I can click math right over here,

03:09.079 --> 03:10.484
move down.

03:10.484 --> 03:12.183
So this function, fn integral,

03:12.183 --> 03:14.621
this is a integral of a function,

03:14.621 --> 03:16.641
or a function integral right over here,

03:16.641 --> 03:18.165
so we press Enter.

03:18.165 --> 03:19.695
And the way that you do it

03:19.695 --> 03:21.239
is you first define the function,

03:21.239 --> 03:22.505
then you put a comma.

03:22.505 --> 03:24.780
Then you say what variable is the variable

03:24.780 --> 03:26.324
that you're integrating with respect to.

03:26.324 --> 03:28.321
And then you put the
bounds of integration.

03:29.181 --> 03:30.217
So I'm gonna write

03:30.217 --> 03:33.136
20sin of

03:33.136 --> 03:36.367
and just cuz it's easier
for me to input x than t,

03:36.367 --> 03:37.714
I'm gonna use x,

03:37.714 --> 03:39.188
but if you just do this

03:39.188 --> 03:40.988
as sin of x squared over 35 dx

03:40.988 --> 03:42.392
you're gonna get the same value

03:42.392 --> 03:44.168
